<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>Without a car, the route turned out to be tricky: a bus from Belgrade to Podgorica, then another bus from Podgorica to Gusinje, and from Gusinje to Vusanje, where I planned to stay, 6 km on foot, mostly on smooth asphalt and a bit of dirt road.</p>
<p>I had no real idea what Prokletije was until the hike itself, even though I&apos;d lived in Montenegro for almost a year. I read the first few links on Google, looked at the pictures and decided to go. I put together a rough plan, again with Claude.</p>
<p>I researched the gear and bought a backpack, a tent, a sleeping bag, a stove, gas and cutlery. I made a list of food, clothes and small things to bring. I&apos;ll describe the gear at the end.</p>
